  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -1220,6 +1220,12 @@ You can adjust name resolution behavior in the Name Resolution section in the <<\n You can control resolution itself by adding a __hosts__ file to your <<ChAppFilesConfigurationSection,personal configuration directory>>.\n You can also edit your system __hosts__ file, but that isn’t generally recommended.\n \n+Another option is to group addresses by their subnet. For instance a common\n+private network is 192.168.0.0/16. Adding this to the __subnets__ file allows\n+Wireshark to show an unknown host in this address range to be part of this\n+network, e.g. \"private:18.145\". A similar file exists for IPv6 subnets.\n+See <<ChAppFilesConfigurationSection>> for more details.\n+\n ==== TCP/UDP Port Name Resolution (Transport Layer)\n \n Try to resolve a TCP/UDP port (e.g., 80) to a human readable name.\n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
      "new_path": "doc/wsug_src/wsug_advanced.adoc",
      "old_path": "doc/wsug_src/wsug_advanced.adoc",
      "a_mode": "100644",
      "b_mode": "100644",
      "new_file": false,
      "renamed_file": false,
      "deleted_file": false,
      "generated_file": false
    },
    {
      "diff": "@@ -176,6 +176,7 @@ _/usr/local/etc_.\n |_services_|Network services.\n |_ss7pcs_|SS7 point code resolution.\n |_subnets_|IPv4 subnet name resolution.\n+|_subnetsipv6_|IPv6 subnet name resolution.\n |_vlans_|VLAN ID name resolution.\n |_wka_|Well-known MAC addresses.\n |===\n@@ -531,23 +532,23 @@ opening a new capture file opens or changing the configuration profile,\n and never written by Wireshark.\n --\n \n-subnets::\n+subnets and subnetsipv6::\n +\n --\n-Wireshark uses the __subnets__ file to translate an IPv4 address into a\n-subnet name.  If no exact match from a __hosts__ file or from DNS is\n-found, Wireshark will attempt a partial match for the subnet of the\n+Wireshark uses the __subnets__ and __subnetsipv6__ files to translate an IP\n+address into a subnet name.  If no exact match from a __hosts__ file or from\n+DNS is found, Wireshark will attempt a partial match for the subnet of the\n address.\n \n-At program start, if there is a _subnets_ file in the personal\n-configuration folder, it is read first.  Then, if there is a _subnets_\n-file in the global configuration folder, that is read; if there is a\n-preference set in both files, the setting in the global preferences file\n-overrides the setting in the personal preference file.\n+At program start, if there is a _subnets_ or _subnetsipv6_ file in the\n+personal configuration folder, it is read first.  Then, if there is a\n+_subnets_ or _subnetsipv6_ file in the global configuration folder, that is\n+read; if there is a preference set in both files, the setting in the global\n+preferences file overrides the setting in the personal preference file.\n \n-Each line in one of these files consists of an IPv4 address, a subnet\n+Each line in one of these files consists of an IP address, a subnet\n mask length separated only by a “/” and a name separated by whitespace.\n-While the address must be a full IPv4 address, any values beyond the\n+While the address must be a full IP address, any values beyond the\n mask length are subsequently ignored.\n \n An example is:\n@@ -556,12 +557,18 @@ An example is:\n 192.168.0.0/24 ws_test_network\n ----\n \n+or\n+\n+----\n+2001:DB8::/32   documentation\n+----\n+\n A partially matched name will be printed as “subnet-name.remaining-address”.\n For example, “192.168.0.1” under the subnet above would be printed as\n “ws_test_network.1”; if the mask length above had been 16 rather than 24, the\n printed address would be “ws_test_network.0.1”.\n \n-The settings from this file are read in at program start, and reloaded when\n+The settings from these files are read in at program start, and reloaded when\n opening a new capture file or changing the configuration profile, and never\n written by Wireshark.\n \n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
      "new_path": "doc/wsug_src/wsug_files.adoc",
      "old_path": "doc/wsug_src/wsug_files.adoc",
